      ":question/problem": "![](images/0b/0b35895b8a5615930aa2d19faf51b60a1c1f110e0b034eb627452b2d518ac749.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a rational function. It has no vertical asymptotes, its $x$-intercept is $(-1, 0)$, and its $y$-intercept is $(0, 2)$. Which of the following could be the equation of the graph?\n\n1. $y = (2x)/((x + 1)(x - 1))$\n2. $y = ((x + 1)^{2})/(x^{2} + 1)$\n3. $y = \\frac{x - 1}{x^{2} + 1}$\n4. $y = (2(x + 1))/(x^{2} + 1)$\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*"
